{
  "name": "leaderboards come in three kinds, and a scorecard is gated three ways",
  "description": "RFC-0008 \u00a71 and \u00a72. search_gates_and_exclusions pins the rank gaps and the inactive toggle; this case adds kind=skill and the scorecard access rules.\n\nA scorecard is the full evidence dossier, so it is the most valuable thing a hirer can read and the thing most worth scraping. Two gates remain: hiring capability, and AssertNotSelf (the second of the three places ADR-0002 requires it).\n\nThe availability gate is NOT one of them any more \u2014 RFC-0008 \u00a71a. A lapsed contributor's scorecard is readable and carries the same active:false block a search result does, because hiding it would mean a hirer could find someone via include_inactive and then be refused the evidence they were looking for. Only not_looking is a 404, and that is an explicit opt-out rather than a stale yes.\n\nThe leaderboard always shows everyone, inactive included, and takes no include_inactive parameter. It is the definitive global ranking; search is the actionable subset of it.",
  "seed": [
    "principals",
    "catalogue",
    "repositories",
    "scored_population"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/leaderboard?kind=skill&skill=go"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "_note": "Dave's Go scores 81 \u2014 higher than anyone here \u2014 and is absent because it is SECONDARY. Standing gates the board; score orders it.",
        "body": {
          "kind": "skill",
          "skill": {
            "slug": "go",
            "name": "Go"
          },
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "entries": [
            {
              "rank": 1,
              "user_id": "<uuid>",
              "display_name": "Alice Okafor",
              "github_login": "aliceok",
              "score": 64.2,
              "active": true
            },
            {
              "rank": 2,
              "user_id": "<uuid>",
              "display_name": "Bob Nakamura",
              "github_login": "bobn",
              "score": 55.0,
              "active": true
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/leaderboard?kind=skill"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 422,
        "body": {
          "error": "invalid_query",
          "items": [
            {
              "field": "skill",
              "reason": "required_for_kind_skill"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/leaderboard?kind=popularity"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 422,
        "body": {
          "error": "invalid_query",
          "items": [
            {
              "field": "kind",
              "reason": "unknown",
              "allowed": [
                "overall",
                "generalist",
                "skill"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A skill nobody holds as primary is an empty board, not a 404. The skill exists; the ranked population does not.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/leaderboard?kind=skill&skill=pr-review"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "body": {
          "kind": "skill",
          "skill": {
            "slug": "pr-review",
            "name": "PR Review"
          },
          "rubric_version": "v1",
          "entries": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
